first of all a happy new year and thx for your answer. I am indeed interested in performing peptide-level inference, since my experimental conditions affect protein processing, so it is a kind of PTM analysis. But I really would like to make sure we are on the same page: Different precursors of the same peptide - in the absence of noise or factors like unexpected modifications - should behave alike in a linear regression? Thought experiment: I would buy 10 synthetic peptides, mix them, pipette a linear dilution series and measure all available precursors by DIA. Will the slope be the same for peptide i in z = 2, 3 , 4, ... or can peptide i | z=2 be different from peptide i | z=3 given the signals allow a high quality regression for both charges. Does the response factor depend on z?

